  "engine_boundary_differences": [
    "Godot mesh import uses its own vertex storage and finite reverse-Z projection. Adapter preserves source shader conventions; bitwise identity is not claimed.",
    "Surfel count/slot dispatch bounds are captured before allocation, matching the reference; trace uses the post-allocation count.",
    "The reference updates surfel irradiance in place. GPU work ordering makes independent runs vary.",
    "New or reset viewports use zero reprojection velocity when history is invalid.",
    "Allocation bounds and workgroup barrier participation are checked; uninitialized or out-of-bounds source behavior is not intentionally reproduced.",
    "SDK-enabled Vulkan Kiln runs NRD RELAX on resolved diffuse and specular radiance; negative temporal specular undershoot is clamped before BRDF composition."
  ],
